For secure PHP coding, always validate and sanitize user inputs to prevent injection attacks. Use prepared statements for database interactions. Ensure error reporting is off in production to avoid exposing sensitive information. Use the `htmlspecialchars()` function to prevent XSS attacks when outputting user-generated content. Here's a sample function that outputs HTML safely:

```php
function printSafeHTML($content) {
    echo htmlspecialchars($content, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8');
}
```

This function ensures that any special characters in the input are properly escaped, making it safe to output as HTML.
